vyatta-cpu-shield (0.2.15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.14 dropped vyatta-cpu-shield-early.service from the package
    entirely: this package's debhelper compat level (9) runs
    dh_systemd_enable/dh_systemd_start, which only auto-installs
    debian/vyatta-cpu-shield.service (or @.service) by that exact name;
    it does not support the debian/package.name.service convention used
    to rename debian/vyatta-cpu-shield.vyatta-cpu-shield-early.service
    (that convention belongs to dh_installsystemd, which this package
    does not use), so the renamed file was silently never installed.
    Ship it via debian/install with an explicit usr/lib/systemd/system
    destination instead, so both units land there and dh_systemd_enable
    still finds and enables it.

 -- Erik Ziegenbalg <erikziege@gmail.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:46:34 +0000

vyatta-cpu-shield (0.2.14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stop shipping vyatta-cpu-shield.service under /lib: it duplicated the
    debian/ unit dh_installsystemd already installs under /usr/lib on
    merged-/usr systems, with stale content (no --startup, no
    system-configure ordering), and dpkg refuses to install a package that
    ships the same aliased path twice with different content.
  * Install vyatta-cpu-shield-early.service via dh_installsystemd
    (debian/vyatta-cpu-shield.vyatta-cpu-shield-early.service) instead of
    debian/install, so it lands under /usr/lib/systemd/system alongside the
    main unit instead of the aliased /lib path.

 -- Erik Ziegenbalg <erikziege@gmail.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:41:49 +0000

